    {
        "content": "<p>I think <code>have := ι.inst</code> as your first line will do it(?)</p>",
        "id": 606440592,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1782379936
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Making it available without such a line... I'm not sure how to do that.</p>",
        "id": 606440749,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1782379979
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, what I'd like is for <code>Qq</code> to perform the destructuring for me. In this example there's only one instance, and so the cost is not too big, but the usecase that inspired my question has a couple more instances which I'd like to avoid projecting at every call site</p>",
        "id": 606441851,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1782380141
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm just not sure if all typeclass inference is happening at the object level in Qq, or if there's some way to hack meta level information in the process. I guess having a way to automatically destructure theses kinds of structures would suffice</p>",
        "id": 606442167,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1782380223
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess I can <code>let {..} ← ι</code> for a reasonable compromise... <span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span></p>",
